It is late Saturday afternoon.
I am standing in my kitchen and preparing dinner.
Today I am cooking a real Mexican meal.
The whole kitchen is already full of steam.
It simply smells wonderful in here.
I wash the tomatoes and chop the rest of the vegetables.
Then I look at my phone.
I open my family's recipe.
I want to be completely sure about the quantities of the ingredients.
I bought the right spices especially for this on Wednesday.
I add them carefully into the large pot.
The sauce is cooking slowly on the stove.
I take a small spoon and taste it.
It is a bit spicy, but very tasty.
That tastes really exactly like home.
I stir everything well one more time and turn down the heat.
Sabine will definitely be here soon.
I am already setting the table for us.
